# string_concat — string.concat lowered via libc malloc/strlen/strcpy/strcat
# (README ss30.2.2). Prints "Hello, world". (todos WS3-015)

StringConcat is project
StringConcat module examplesStringConcat
StringConcat target console
StringConcat entry main

examplesStringConcat is module
examplesStringConcat path examples.stringConcat
examplesStringConcat exports main
examplesStringConcat purpose "Concatenate two strings and print the result"
examplesStringConcat invariant "main is the only entry operation"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32
ExitCode purpose "Process exit status"

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout
stdoutWriter purpose "Allow controlled writes to standard output"

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memory heap yes
main async no
main purpose "Concatenate a greeting and print it"
main invariant "Writes exactly: Hello, world"
main let greeting immutable String "Hello, "
main let subject immutable String "world"
main let okCode immutable ExitCode 0
main do joinText
main do writeJoined
main return okCode

joinText is call
joinText in main
joinText invokes string.concat
joinText arg left String greeting
joinText arg right String subject
joinText out message String

writeJoined is call
writeJoined in main
writeJoined invokes console.writeLine
writeJoined arg text String message
